            "category": "bug",
            "confidence": 62,
            "evidence": "`_global_type_lookup[builtins.sentinel] = st.builds(builtins.sentinel, st.text())` \u2014 st.text() produces arbitrarily many distinct names, each creating a permanently interned sentinel.",
            "file_path": "hypothesis/src/hypothesis/strategies/_internal/types.py",
            "finding": "Registering `builtins.sentinel` with `st.builds(builtins.sentinel, st.text())` will create a new interned sentinel object per generated name. PEP 661-style sentinels are cached globally by name, so drawing arbitrary text values leaks an unbounded number of module-level sentinel objects across a test run.",
            "line": 1008,
            "severity": "medium",
            "source_refs": [
              "types.py:1008-1013"
            ],
            "suggested_fix": "Restrict to a small fixed set of names, e.g. `st.sampled_from([\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"]).map(builtins.sentinel)`, or use `st.just(builtins.sentinel(\"hypothesis_sentinel\"))`."
          },
          "finding_index": 0,
          "publish_decision": "suppress",
          "suppression_reason": "low_confidence"
        },
        {
